================================================================================================
SYNTHESIS
  1. The exact all-w>=15 maxima match the short low-head scout rows:
       k=8 w=21, k=9 w=68, k=10 w=22, k=11 w=16, k=12 w=71.
  2. The positive endpoint numerator satisfies maxS <= 1289/980 < 1.316
     across k=8..12.  Therefore maxS/15 is below 0.453 of the cap margin
     in every consecutive binding row.
  3. This gives an exact finite certificate for the consec-base single-far
     branch.  It is compatible with HYP-2785: the modulus is endpoint-period
     sized, not residue-only mod 7.
  4. Remaining proof work: prove near-cap bases reduce to this consecutive
     endpoint-period certificate, or give each non-consec base a plateau-slack
     ledger against its own endpoint numerator.

